A question in a recent thread makes me think about harm done by
beartraps.  That bloody tool is really bad, but in NH it seems
to just hinder a victim slightly in movement, no damage is done
(AFAIK).

Shouldn't it at least let you lose some (5) HPs at the moment it
closes?  And if you want to leave it through simple movement you
would be losing a HP per move until you come free?  These small
changes would make it IMO more interesting (and more realisitic
if that matters).  You would not be injured if you leave it by
teleport, polymorphing into amorphous creatures, etc.

Untrapping it with high STR and sufficient DEX could be allowed.
When you fail untrapping yourself the trap would close again and
cause another loss of 5 or so HPs.

Would make beartraps more challenging, IMO.  What do you think?

